  "ref": "LEV.13.10",
  "review_notes": [
    "mihyat basar hay is aligned quick (mihyah) / raw (hay) / flesh (basar), which is how the chapter renders the same two lemmas elsewhere: basar hay is raw flesh at 13.14, 13.15 and 13.16, and mihyat ha-mmikhwah is the quick flesh* at 13.24 with flesh italicized as an ASV supply. The earlier reading of this verse had raw on mihyah and quick on hay; the chapter reconciliation reversed it because no morphological difference licenses the swap, and the resulting units are contiguous.",
    "The competing reading recorded at the verse pass, which gives quick raw wholly to mihyah and leaves hay unrepresented, is still available but is not taken: hay has its own written English in every other verse of the chapter."
  ]
